module v2.test.manual.forensics_6280_tokenize_reject_locus

import extdeps.filesystem.filesystem_io
import v2.compiler.tokenize { tokenize }
import v2.compiler.parse { parse_module }
import v2.extdeps.languages.dag { dag_language_model_wave1 }
import v2.std.diagnostic { Accepted, Rejected }

data forensics_6280_task_note: String = "Task: 'Forensics: 6280 memo commit flips census tokenize-reject to parse-reject on 01_tokenize.dag - name the mechanism.' Ground truth (this file's own witnesses, re-run independently 5x across processes, plus a v2.lens.enforcement.grammar_coverage direct-call replication on PR #6252's own branch): src/v1/01_tokenize.dag TOKENIZES CLEAN and REJECTS AT PARSE. It never rejected at tokenize on either side of #6280 -- #6280 only threads a packrat memo table through 02_parse.dag and never touches tokenize/lex code, so it cannot be the cause of a tokenize-reject verdict that ground truth says never existed."

data forensics_6280_mechanism_note: String = "FINAL REPORT, part 1 -- STATIC WALL-HOLES (joint finding with sunny-wren-799, cross-session, 2026-07-05): a constructor-owner collision wall gap, not a #6280 regression. The per-file constructor-owner ruling (v1_compiler_infer.rs build_imported_variants/unique_imported_variant_owner) only assigns a deterministic single owner to a bare constructor name if that name appears in one of the importing module's OWN explicit specific-name imports -- it never checks the rest of the loaded corpus for other same-named variants declared elsewhere. TWO CONFIRMED INSTANCES: (a) IN the witness closure -- dag/std/markup.dag declares a MarkupSerializeResult.Rejected variant with field reason of type String; src/v2/std/diagnostic.dag declares an Outcome.Rejected variant with field diagnostics of type NonEmptyDiagnostics. src/v2/compiler/02_parse.dag explicitly imports Rejected alongside Accepted and is covered; src/v2/compiler/01_tokenize.dag imports Accepted but NOT Rejected despite constructing a bare Rejected record at lines 503 and 519 -- uncovered. This site IS reachable from the grammar_coverage witness's transitive import closure (both Rejected owners load together whenever a census-style tool runs with --source-root dag and --source-root src/v2). (b) OUT of this particular witness closure but independently verified -- src/v2/extdeps/languages/ptx.dag imports a long name list from v2.std.grammar that omits Terminal, yet constructs a bare Terminal record with fields token_class/stamp at line 128 (ptx_grammar_terminal); dag/std/disposition.dag independently declares an unrelated Terminal variant with field reason. Same missing-import shape as the Rejected gap, confirmed by BFS of the witness's actual closure to NOT be this witness's live trigger, but a second concrete, verifiable instance of the identical pattern elsewhere in the tree. HAZARD SURFACE: a closure census of the grammar_coverage witness's entry found 31 genuine duplicate top-level names across the dag-tree/v2-tree fork (Terminal, Char, Optional, Holds, Empty, FreeMonoid, Nat, List, Map, Bool, nat_compare, qualified_name_from_segment_list, construction_justification, among others) -- each is a candidate site for this same wall-hole shape and the complete suspect set is enumerable by grepping, for each name, for bare construction/match sites in closure modules that do not import that name."

data forensics_6280_quarantine_note: String = "FINAL REPORT, part 2 -- METHODOLOGY CORRECTION (document prominently: this was assumed wrong by everyone investigating, including sunny-wren-799, and it invalidated multiple earlier confound theories): gunbc run resolves only the TRANSITIVE IMPORT CLOSURE reachable from --entry, NOT the whole --source-root tree. A file sitting under --source-root that nothing imports is never loaded and cannot affect resolution, no matter how many --source-root flags are passed. This was confirmed two ways: (i) an unimported decoy fixture in this session's own synthetic reproducer had zero effect until actually imported into the closure; (ii) sunny-wren-799 BFS-walked the real witness's closure on the real corpus (61 files, matching the observed source count) and found neither dag/std/markup.dag nor dag/gunbc/workflow/types.dag in it -- meaning the markup/diagnostic Rejected collision, while real and structurally identical to the wall-hole, is NOT what the witness's own resolution sees; only v2.std.diagnostic's Rejected is in-closure there, so a same-content, cross-process true/false flip on that exact witness cannot be explained by an ambiguous Rejected owner at all. Both the earlier 'CI-timeout-window' and 'copied-probe-files-into-the-tree' confound theories collapsed once this was established, since presence under a source root is not the same as presence in the resolved closure.

FINAL REPORT, part 3 -- VARIANCE (mechanism still OPEN): observed directly on the real corpus -- sunny-wren-799's battery recorded 1 flip in 4 same-config, same-tree, same-binary, same-entry runs (additional samples running). The interpreter is single-threaded in stage0 (zero rayon/par_iter/spawn), which rules out thread-race nondeterminism, leaving Rust's per-process randomized HashMap RandomState seed as the only remaining variance source consistent with same-content, same-process-count divergence -- some multi-candidate iteration point in an un-walled fallback or environment-merge path (candidate sites enumerable from the 31-name duplicate closure census in part 1) whose per-process hash-order tie-break occasionally resolves differently. NOT YET LOCATED: this session built and ran a synthetic reproducer across ~70 executions (2-owner and 3-owner collision shape, up to 46 loaded sources matching the real corpus's ~45-60 range, plain-position and generic-instantiation shapes mirroring Outcome<T> exactly) and never reproduced a flip -- every synthetic construction site got its owner PINNED (by a declared return type or an import elsewhere in the same small closure) before any fallback could run, meaning the real path exercises a resolution point this reproducer has not yet replicated structurally. Reported as an honest negative, not asserted as a disproof: the wall-hole shape is real and duplicated (part 1), the variance is real and observed (sunny-wren-799's battery), but the causal link between them for THIS specific witness is not yet a closed loop -- pending further battery samples and a synthetic shape that actually exercises the fallback.

FINAL REPORT, part 4 -- QUARANTINE BOUNDARY + PRACTICAL NOTE: any census/lens verdict produced by a tool whose entry-closure includes a bare, un-imported coproduct constructor colliding in name with an unrelated type also in that closure is UNTRUSTED for the stage that constructs it, until the wall covers un-imported bare constructors. Known instances: v2.lens.enforcement.grammar_coverage's tokenize-stage verdict for src/v1/01_tokenize.dag (PR #6252, in-closure Rejected collision) and any ptx.dag-reaching witness for its Terminal construction (out-of-closure for the grammar_coverage witness specifically, but live wherever ptx.dag IS reachable). Practical constraint: verifying a census pin by N repeated runs costs approximately 500s per run on the current interpreted tokenizer -- unaffordable for confirmation-grade N until calm-bear's string_head fix lands (quoted at ~125s per run) -- this is sequencing input for the operator, not a blocker on this report.

FINAL REPORT, part 5 -- FIX DIRECTION ONLY (not landed here, needs operator sign-off per the constructor-owner ruling's own lane): (a) wall extension -- a bare constructor with >=2 candidate owners visible in the loaded corpus and NO owning explicit import should be a typed VariantCollision refusal at resolve time, not a silent fallback pick; this is an engine-lane fix (v1_compiler_infer.rs / v1_compiler_resolve.rs). (b) defense-in-depth -- deterministic (sorted, not raw-HashMap) iteration order at whatever fallback/env-merge site currently exercises RandomState-seeded iteration, so that even before (a) lands, a same-content run is at least reproducible rather than seed-sensitive. Neither is landed by this PR -- no rename of markup.Rejected, no v1_rt.rs sort, no ptx.dag import fix -- these are proposals with receipts, awaiting sign-off."

type Verdict
  = TokenizeReject { reason: Symbol }
  | ParseReject { reason: Symbol }
  | ParsedClean

fn forensics_6280_probe_verdict() -> Verdict {
  let lm = dag_language_model_wave1()
  let source_text = filesystem_read(path: "src/v1/01_tokenize.dag").content
  match tokenize(text: source_text, file: ^forensics_6280_probe_file_anchor, rules: lm.lex) {
    Rejected { diagnostics: d } => TokenizeReject { reason: d.head.reason }
    Accepted { value: ts, diagnostics: _ } =>
      match parse_module(tokens: ts, grammar: lm.grammar) {
        Rejected { diagnostics: d } => ParseReject { reason: d.head.reason }
        Accepted { value: _, diagnostics: _ } => ParsedClean
      }
  }
}

fn forensics_6280_witness_ground_truth_is_not_tokenize_reject() -> Bool {
  match forensics_6280_probe_verdict() {
    TokenizeReject { reason: _ } => false
    ParseReject { reason: _ } => true
    ParsedClean => true
  }
}

fn forensics_6280_witness_ground_truth_is_parse_reject() -> Bool {
  match forensics_6280_probe_verdict() {
    TokenizeReject { reason: _ } => false
    ParseReject { reason: _ } => true
    ParsedClean => false
  }
}
